WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.564
Peter had a birthday—his tenth.

2
00:00:16.565 --> 00:00:18.447
Father was at work.

3
00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:23.882
But his sisters, Bobbie and Phyllis, and his mother all gave him presents in the morning.

4
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:29.449
One of these presents was a model engine, and Peter was overjoyed.

5
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.903
Peter's joy lasted for three days until the engine suddenly went bang!

6
00:00:33.904 --> 00:00:35.747
The engine was broken.

7
00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:37.968
Peter was very unhappy.

8
00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:44.097
His sisters said he had cried, but Peter insisted his eyes were red from a cold.

9
00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:49.429
When Father came home that evening, Peter told him the story of the broken engine.

10
00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.092
Father looked at the toy engine carefully.

11
00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:57.319
"Hmm," said Father. The children waited impatiently.

12
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.336
"Is there any hope?" asked Peter.

13
00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:06.601
"Yes, it can be fixed with some tools—but not tonight," said Father cheerfully.

14
00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:11.097
"Let's wait till Saturday and you can all help me fix it."

15
00:01:11.098 --> 00:01:15.581
"Can girls help to fix engines?" Peter asked doubtfully.

16
00:01:15.582 --> 00:01:22.212
"Of course! Girls are just as clever as boys, and don't you forget it!" Father said.

17
00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:25.401
"How would you like to be an engine driver, Phyllis?"

18
00:01:25.402 --> 00:01:32.875
"No, my face would always be dirty," said Phyllis.

19
00:01:32.876 --> 00:01:36.106
"I would just love it," said Bobbie.

20
00:01:36.107 --> 00:01:39.633
"Can I be an engine driver when I grow up, Father?"

21
00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.871
"Yes, we'll help you!" Father replied.

22
00:01:42.872 --> 00:01:45.807
Suddenly there was a knock at the door.

23
00:01:45.808 --> 00:01:48.683
"Who's that?" said Father.

24
00:01:48.684 --> 00:01:52.385
Mother came in and said that two gentlemen wanted to see Father.

25
00:01:52.386 --> 00:01:55.413
"They're in the next room," she added.

26
00:01:55.414 --> 00:02:00.830
"I hope they leave soon because it's nearly the children's bedtime."

27
00:02:00.831 --> 00:02:03.866
But the visitors stayed until late.

28
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:07.948
Mother told the children a story about a princess with green eyes.

29
00:02:07.949 --> 00:02:12.297
It was difficult for the children to listen because voices came from the next room.

30
00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.221
Father's voice sounded louder than usual.

31
00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:20.176
He even sounded angry.

32
00:02:20.177 --> 00:02:22.668
Ruth, the maid, came in.

33
00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:26.091
"He wants you to go in, ma'am," she said to Mother.

34
00:02:26.092 --> 00:02:28.540
"I think he's had bad news.

35
00:02:28.541 --> 00:02:31.079
Be ready for the worst."

36
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.591
So Mother went into the next room, and there was more talking.

37
00:02:35.592 --> 00:02:39.009
Later Mother came back, and her face was pale.

38
00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.304
"It's bedtime," she said. "Ruth will put you to bed."

39
00:02:44.305 --> 00:02:49.413
"But you promised we could stay up with Father!" said Phyllis.

40
00:02:49.414 --> 00:02:53.889
"Father had to leave—on business," said Mother.

41
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.861
The children kissed her and went to bed. Bobbie lingered.

42
00:02:57.862 --> 00:03:02.564
She hugged Mother and whispered, "It wasn't bad news, was it, Mommy?

43
00:03:02.565 --> 00:03:05.396
Did someone . . . die?"

44
00:03:05.397 --> 00:03:14.298
"Nobody died, no," said Mother, and she almost seemed to push Bobbie away.

45
00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.833
When the children woke up the next morning, Mother was gone.

46
00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:24.622
"I think something awful has happened," said Peter during breakfast.

47
00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:28.471
"I asked Ruth, and she said we'll find out soon."

48
00:03:28.472 --> 00:03:33.035
"You should have waited to ask Mother!" Bobbie said angrily.

49
00:03:33.036 --> 00:03:36.234
It was seven o'clock in the evening when Mother came home.

50
00:03:36.235 --> 00:03:38.165
She looked worn-out.

51
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:41.947
After she rested and had a cup of tea, she said,

52
00:03:41.948 --> 00:03:45.877
"My darlings, I want to tell you something.

53
00:03:45.878 --> 00:03:50.331
Those men did bring very bad news last night.

54
00:03:50.332 --> 00:03:52.960
Father won't be here for some time.

55
00:03:52.961 --> 00:03:56.972
I am very worried, and I want you to help me.

56
00:03:56.973 --> 00:04:01.280
You can help me by being good and not quarreling."

57
00:04:01.281 --> 00:04:04.178
The children wondered why Father had to leave.

58
00:04:04.179 --> 00:04:10.866
What could have happened?
